    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.ai\n\n### Question\n\nthis is my  options, and i want to use vab, and vib, to select  chinese bracket as a textobject, but \r\nvab and vib will all select  outer textobject, looks like inner （ textobject has no use, how can i fix this?\r\n```\r\n    opts.custom_textobjects.b = {\r\n        { \"%b()\", \"%b[]\", \"%b{}\", ai.gen_spec.pair(\"（\", \"）\"), ai.gen_spec.pair(\"【\", \"】\") }, \r\n        \"^.().*().$\",\r\n      }\r\n```\r\n",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.ai</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">this is my  options, and i want to use vab, and vib, to select  chinese bracket as a textobject, but<br>\nvab and vib will all select  outer textobject, looks like inner （ textobject has no use, how can i fix this?</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"    opts.custom_textobjects.b = {\n        { &quot;%b()&quot;, &quot;%b[]&quot;, &quot;%b{}&quot;, ai.gen_spec.pair(&quot;（&quot;, &quot;）&quot;), ai.gen_spec.pair(&quot;【&quot;, &quot;】&quot;) }, \n        &quot;^.().*().$&quot;,\n      }\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">    opts.custom_textobjects.b = {\n        { \"%b()\", \"%b[]\", \"%b{}\", ai.gen_spec.pair(\"（\", \"）\"), ai.gen_spec.pair(\"【\", \"】\") }, \n        \"^.().*().$\",\n      }\n</code></pre></div>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.ai\nQuestion\nthis is my  options, and i want to use vab, and vib, to select  chinese bracket as a textobject, but\nvab and vib will all select  outer textobject, looks like inner （ textobject has no use, how can i fix this?\n    opts.custom_textobjects.b = {\n        { \"%b()\", \"%b[]\", \"%b{}\", ai.gen_spec.pair(\"（\", \"）\"), ai.gen_spec.pair(\"【\", \"】\") }, \n        \"^.().*().$\",\n      }",
    "category": {
        "createdAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z",
        "description": "Ask the community for help",
        "emoji": ":pray:",
        "emojiHTML": "<div>🙏</div>",
        "id": "DIC_kwDOFoksYM4CAgqN",
        "isAnswerable": true,
        "name": "Q&A",
        "slug": "q-a",
        "updatedAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z"
    },
    "closed": true,
    "closedAt": "2025-09-28T11:28:06Z",
    "comment_count": 1,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/119845045?u=9e2489487d1e983158fa9026e290027a273bd2be&v=4",
                "login": "drowning-cat",
                "resourcePath": "/drowning-cat",
                "url": "https://github.com/drowning-cat"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "In your case, I’d do it this way, though maybe @echasnovski has a better solution:\r\n\r\n> [!WARNING]\r\n> It seems your quotes are treated as multiple chars, so `%b【】` doesn’t work in Lua.\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nb = {\r\n  {\r\n    MiniAi.gen_spec.pair(\"【\", \"】\"),\r\n    MiniAi.gen_spec.pair(\"(\", \")\", { type = \"balanced\" }),\r\n    MiniAi.gen_spec.pair(\"[\", \"]\", { type = \"balanced\" }),\r\n    MiniAi.gen_spec.pair(\"{\", \"}\", { type = \"balanced\" }),\r\n  },\r\n},\r\n```",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">In your case, I’d do it this way, though maybe <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/echasnovski/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski\">@echasnovski</a> has a better solution:</p>\n<div class=\"markdown-alert markdown-alert-warning\" dir=\"auto\"><p class=\"markdown-alert-title\" dir=\"auto\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-alert mr-2\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M6.457 1.047c.659-1.234 2.427-1.234 3.086 0l6.082 11.378A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 14.082 15H1.918a1.75 1.75 0 0 1-1.543-2.575Zm1.763.707a.25.25 0 0 0-.44 0L1.698 13.132a.25.25 0 0 0 .22.368h12.164a.25.25 0 0 0 .22-.368Zm.53 3.996v2.5a.75.75 0 0 1-1.5 0v-2.5a.75.75 0 0 1 1.5 0ZM9 11a1 1 0 1 1-2 0 1 1 0 0 1 2 0Z\"></path></svg>Warning</p><p dir=\"auto\">It seems your quotes are treated as multiple chars, so <code class=\"notranslate\">%b【】</code> doesn’t work in Lua.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"b = {\n  {\n    MiniAi.gen_spec.pair(&quot;【&quot;, &quot;】&quot;),\n    MiniAi.gen_spec.pair(&quot;(&quot;, &quot;)&quot;, { type = &quot;balanced&quot; }),\n    MiniAi.gen_spec.pair(&quot;[&quot;, &quot;]&quot;, { type = &quot;balanced&quot; }),\n    MiniAi.gen_spec.pair(&quot;{&quot;, &quot;}&quot;, { type = &quot;balanced&quot; }),\n  },\n},\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-smi\">b</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n  {\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">MiniAi</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">gen_spec</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">pair</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>【<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>】<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>),\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">MiniAi</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">gen_spec</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">pair</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>(<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>)<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, { <span class=\"pl-smi\">type</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>balanced<span class=\"pl-pds\">\" </span></span>}),\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">MiniAi</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">gen_spec</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">pair</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>[<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>]<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, { <span class=\"pl-smi\">type</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>balanced<span class=\"pl-pds\">\" </span></span>}),\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">MiniAi</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">gen_spec</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">pair</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>{<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>}<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, { <span class=\"pl-smi\">type</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>balanced<span class=\"pl-pds\">\" </span></span>}),\n  },\n},</pre></div>",
            "bodyText": "In your case, I’d do it this way, though maybe @echasnovski has a better solution:\nWarningIt seems your quotes are treated as multiple chars, so %b【】 doesn’t work in Lua.\n\nb = {\n  {\n    MiniAi.gen_spec.pair(\"【\", \"】\"),\n    MiniAi.gen_spec.pair(\"(\", \")\", { type = \"balanced\" }),\n    MiniAi.gen_spec.pair(\"[\", \"]\", { type = \"balanced\" }),\n    MiniAi.gen_spec.pair(\"{\", \"}\", { type = \"balanced\" }),\n  },\n},",
